// stmt-permute swaps a block's value with the let before it, making a
// block that ends in a let, which the checker refuses by rule.
// command: design/review-2026-10-26/repro/fuzz-mutate-run-typemorph-one.sh \
//            design/review-2026-10-26/repro/fuzz-mutate-stmt-permute-trailing-let.gx
// expected: BASE accept and no FLIP (stmt-permute is acceptance-preserving)
// observed: FLIP stmt-permute#1 N: a block's value is its last statement,
//           and a let has none: end the block with an expression
//           MUTANT { let a = 1; 42; let b = 2 }
// The same flip came from 5 of 138 sampled regression pins
// (e.g. findings/flip-jun2026/02_dead_bottom_stmt.gx).
{ let a = 1; let b = 2; 42 }
